EvidenceMap maps each requirement or standard to how we meet it and the documents that prove it, drawn as a mapping with leader lines and file-shaped chips, for the validation lead asking "where is the proof?".

- Data: a `table` block with `"as": "evidence"`. `cols`: requirement, how we meet it, then evidence columns. An evidence column whose every cell is a page link becomes the row's quiet link; every other one becomes document chips (cells split on ";", first letter capitalized), grouped under the column name when there are several.
- References are not files. An evidence column named in the block's `ref` (column names or indexes), or whose every filled cell is only clause numbers ("11.10(e)", "7; 17", "11.50, 11.70"), prints on the fan as mono text (`li.aq-evidence__doc.is-ref` > `.aq-evidence__rk` standard name when there are several columns, `.aq-evidence__clause` Mono 500 15/26 `ink`), with the tick and arrow but no sheet. A requirement written "Change control · ISO 9001 6.3, 8.5.6" shows the part after " · " as a mono reference line under the name (`.aq-evidence__ref`, Mono 13/20 `ink-muted`). A "how" cell whose every ";" part opens with a clause number ("6.7 no dead legs; 6.10 WFI > 70 °C") becomes a clause list (`ul.aq-evidence__clauses`, numbers in a mono column).
- Markup (`blocks/evidence.js`): a real table. `.aq-evidence` > `table.aq-evidence__table` with a `thead` of column names (Geist 500 14/20 `ink-muted` on `surface-sunken`, sentence case) and rows `tr.aq-evidence__row`: `th.aq-evidence__t[scope=row]` (`.aq-evidence__n` the shared mono index, aria-hidden; `.aq-evidence__name`), `td.aq-evidence__how`, `td.aq-evidence__proof` (optional `.aq-evidence__k` captions as eyebrows, `ul.aq-evidence__docs` of `li.aq-evidence__doc` > `.aq-evidence__file`, then `.aq-evidence__go` link).
- Desktop: the requirement is an `h3` (Geist 500 20/28) with the hanging mono index (13 px `ink-subtle`) and a `line` hairline on its right edge; "how" in Geist 16/26 `ink-muted`. A `line` leader runs from that hairline to "how" (ending in a small `flow` dot), and from "how" into a `line` spine that fans out to every file chip, each tick ending in a small `flow` arrowhead. File chips are small sheets: mono 12 px, `line` outline on `surface-raised`, square corners, the top-right corner folded (CSS `clip-path` plus a `surface-sunken` flap, no gradient), no images.
- Phones (`@container (max-width: 860px)`): rows stack (index and requirement at 18/26, how, files). A left connector runs down from the number past "how" into the same fan of file chips.
- Ground: the section's `surface`; tokens only, so it reads in either theme. Supports `fold`.
- For a list of documents without requirements use DocList; for standards alone, StandardsGrid.

## Motion

`motion.js`: each requirement reads in, then the link draws from claim to proof: the leader and "how we meet it" wipe in left to right from the requirement's rule, the fan wipes on into the proof column and the file chips (or clause references) slide onto their ticks one by one. Phones: the same order down the left connector. Rows play in reading order as they scroll in; nothing under reduced motion.
